{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310777,"nonce":"qQ/MNZWyil89JZwau6LpRPvWXEI=","title":"2026-06-12 AOT'd llama-chat-server benched vs JIT via bench_server.sh SERVER_BIN mode — cold start solved (0.37s ready / 0.60s TTFT ...","message":"After the AOT interface-dispatch fix ([[bugs_aot_iface_dispatch_fixed]]),\n`rayzor aot` on nue/examples/llama-chat-server produces a working TCP\nserver binary. Benched with the same bench_server.sh harness via the new\n`SERVER_BIN=/path/to/binary` mode (commit pending; bench script edit).\n\n**Numbers (M1 Pro, Llama 3.2 1B Q4_K_M, 3 reqs × 808-tok cap, 15s cooldowns):**\n\n| metric | JIT (1/30/5, start_interp=false) | AOT -O2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| ready (launch→listen) | 0.57s warm / **8.43s cold-cache** | **0.36-0.48s always** |\n| cold_ttft | 0.79s warm / 8.67s cold | **0.58-0.60s** |\n| decode median (profile OFF) | 81.38 (σ=0.65) | 77.6-78.1 (9 runs, σ≈0.3-0.65) |\n| decode median (profile ON) | 78.71 | 76.3 |\n| prefill_med / tokenize / p95-step | 183-204ms / 0.4-0.7ms / 13.0-14.5ms | 188-202ms / 0.5ms / 13.5-14ms |\n\n**Conclusions:**\n- Cold start is SOLVED by AOT: no compile-before-listen, no BLADE cache\n  warm-up (the JIT's first-run 8.4s penalty took TWO runs to fully warm).\n  TTFT from process launch is ~0.6s = model load (0.3s) + prefill (0.2s).\n- Steady decode: AOT trails the Cranelift-JIT plateau by ~3-4%, uniform\n  per-step (not tails, not prefill — phase splits identical). `-O3`\n  AOT: no change (77.27). Cause unidentified; candidates: system-LLVM\n  codegen of hot Haxe orchestration loops vs Cranelift, the env-prefixed\n  vtable thunk hop. NOT worth chasing before kernel-level levers.\n- DECODE_PROFILE=1 itself costs ~2-3 tok/s (Sys.time per phase per\n  token) — never compare profile-on vs profile-off numbers.\n- 90 tok/s is NOT reachable via compilation mode: decode is ~87%\n  matmul_qt_t at M1 ILP saturation ([[perf_kernel_breakdown_full_2026_06_07]]);\n  rayzor is at ~93% of llama.cpp CPU. Remaining levers are\n  kernel/threading, not AOT-vs-JIT.\n- Requant/eager-quant thermal thesis: requant runs once inside\n  LlamaArch.build pre-listen (~0.1-0.2s) in BOTH modes; no coupling with\n  decode thermals observed (σ\u003c0.7 across all clean runs both modes).\n\n**Anomalies + gotchas:**\n- One-off: very first execution of a fresh AOT binary had one stalled\n  request (9.2 tok/s for 62s); never recurred across 8 subsequent runs.\n  Suspect first-run page-in/codesign verification. Watch for recurrence.\n- Stale BLADE cache across COMPILER rebuilds poisons JIT compile\n  (`can't resolve symbol append` panic + IMPORT[Int32]/FPHelper field\n  errors) when bench runs NO_CACHE=false. Same class as\n  [[bugs_rayzor_cache_scrub]]; scrub .rayzor after any rayzor rebuild.\n  Underlying defect: BLADE cache key doesn't include compiler build id.\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\ncd nue/examples/llama-chat-server\nrayzor aot -o llama-server-aot          # manifest mode picks up class-paths + nue-plugins\nSERVER_BIN=./llama-server-aot STREAM=true PREFILL_MORSELS=true REQUANT_LM_HEAD=1 ./bench_server.sh\n```\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_aot_server_cold_start` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}